  "sourceInterpretation": "Official image reports ESP-IDFv6.1-dirty,exact private source revision unknown. Public rtc_time.c/clock LL/register headers fixed to fff9895c82d744c7237be8847347bdd1b07c6643. Fixed rtc_time.c counts XTAL ticks over target cycles; generated CALI_MAX prose inconsistently calls its unit XTAL_CLK. This model follows executable LL/caller behavior,not that misleading sentence.",
  "semantics": {
    "measurement": "Counts explicit XTAL ticks over MAX target cycles with programmed divisor+1. One-shot READY,periodic valid/result,timeout after threshold exceeded. Reads/RO writes cannot finish a measurement.",
    "clocks": "Supported existing functional MPLL/CPLL,SYS/APB/MEM,136kHz nominalRC_SLOW and40MHz XTAL. Target gate produces no edges and can time out. Register reset preserves separate mux; APB gate blocks MMIO.",
    "developmentTiming": "Separate --rtc-calibration-from-cpu. One nominal CPU quantum per scheduler round; fractional XTAL conversion preserved across clock frequency changes. Existing --rtc-timer-from-cpu is unchanged. Strict default has no implicit calibration ticks.",
    "unsupported": [
      "Unconnected BBPLL/APLL,RC_FAST digital routing,external32K/pad and per-core gates",
      "Zero-cycle requests outside fixed LL contract",
      "Timeout reset-pulse width and physical sampling/jitter; periodic windows restart zero phase and round ideal measurement upward",
      "General-purpose TIMG timers",
      "Modem power/clocks,remaining Plus peripherals and parallel EPD"
    ]
  },
